WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.711
A Boolean value is either true or false Python can
also convert other values

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:11.395
into Boolean form Zero and an empty string behave
like false while nonzero numbers

00:00:11.421 --> 00:00:17.309
and nonempty strings behave like true For now the
important goal is simply

00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:22.785
to observe the pattern In the next module Boolean
values will become the basis for

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:26.482
conditions such as if sales are above a target or if
a record is missing

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:32.152
a required value Run the examples and compare zero
with one and an

00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:37.102
empty string with a string that contains text This
gives you an early preview of

00:00:37.129 --> 00:00:39.181
how Python will later make decisions
